write the seated cart behind the draw

Every cart that seated stalled the draw for one frame as the game came
up: on the Flip, update 43-49 ms in the frame before "first frame shown",
every insert in the traces. Seating records the cart in slot.state, and the
recents too when the cart was not already at their head, and each of those
was `persist`: the slot-state writer flushed, then slot.state written and
synced on the draw thread. Two writes to the card in one frame.

Both now go through `persist_soon`, the writer thread upstream already
uses for the settings. It keeps only the latest state, and every write that
does have to land in line -- the eject's, the save states' -- flushes it
first. No save of the game itself goes through here; the worst a power
loss in the few milliseconds before the writer lands can do is boot to the
previous seated cart or recents order.

The eject's own write at the press (35-94 ms, the game's save and state)
and the emulator thread's join when the cart leaves (~20 ms) are left as
they are: the first is what keeps a save from being lost, and the second
is what keeps two instances of a core from running at once.

Five integration tests read slot.state straight off the card after a cart
seats or leaves; they now flush the writer first, as boot.rs already does
for the settings. The slot crate's integration tests otherwise fail as
they did before this patch -- 25 of 986 on main, core picker and 4:3
layout expectations the port changed long ago -- and none newly.

Applies on top of 0053, upstream 91499a9.

diff --git a/crates/slot/src/app.rs b/crates/slot/src/app.rs
--- a/crates/slot/src/app.rs
+++ b/crates/slot/src/app.rs
@@ -3721,6 +3721,11 @@
         self.persist();
     }
 
+    /// Written behind the draw: a cart seating wrote slot.state twice in line,
+    /// the recents and then the cart, and on the Flip that was a 46 ms frame
+    /// as the game's first one came up. Every save of the game itself is
+    /// written elsewhere; this is the seated cart and the recents, and the
+    /// next write that has to land in line flushes this one first.
     fn record_cart(&mut self, cart: Option<String>) {
         let platform = self.seated_cart().map(|c| c.platform);
         if let (Some(stem), Some(platform)) = (&cart, platform) {
@@ -3729,7 +3734,7 @@
                 let stem = stem.clone();
                 self.state.played(platform, &stem);
                 self.restock_recents();
-                self.persist();
+                self.persist_soon();
             }
         }
         if self.state.cart == cart && self.state.cart_platform == platform {
@@ -3737,7 +3742,7 @@
         }
         self.state.cart = cart;
         self.state.cart_platform = platform;
-        self.persist();
+        self.persist_soon();
     }
 
     fn persist(&self) {
